---
// English version of src/pages/politique-de-protection-des-donnees.astro — keep both aligned.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SOCIETE as S } from '../../data/societe';
---
<Base
  title="Data protection policy | digitags.work"
  description="digitags.work data protection policy: data collected, purposes, legal bases, retention periods, processors, transfers outside the EU and your rights (GDPR)."
>
  <section class="page-hero" style="padding-bottom: 20px;">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>The Hub's data protection policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">What we collect, why, for how long, and how to exercise your rights.</p>
      <p class="post-meta" style="justify-content: flex-start;">Updated 21 November 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="container prose">
    <h2>Data controller</h2>
    <p>Personal data collected on www.digitags.work is processed by <strong>{S.denomination}</strong>, {S.formeEn}, {S.siege}, {S.rcs} (see our <a href="/en/legal-notice">legal notice</a>). For any question about your data: <a href={`mailto:${S.email}`}>{S.email}</a>.</p>
    <p>This policy applies under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR, EU Regulation 2016/679) and the French Data Protection Act of 6 January 1978 as amended ("Informatique et Libertés"). We have not appointed a data protection officer: the address above is dedicated to these requests.</p>

    <h2>Visiting the site: no tracking cookies</h2>
    <p>We measure audience with <strong>Plausible Analytics</strong>, a European tool that uses <strong>no cookies</strong>, collects no personal data and cannot follow you from one site to another. Statistics are aggregated and anonymous (pages viewed, referring sites, country, device type). That's why the site shows no consent banner.</p>
    <p>The site sets no advertising or audience-measurement cookies. Only strictly necessary items may be stored in your browser: remembering that you closed the information message (local storage) and, on private pages reserved for our clients or our team, a session or access cookie. These items are exempt from consent.</p>
    <p>Our hosting provider, Cloudflare, technically processes visitors' IP addresses to deliver pages and protect the site against attacks, on the basis of our legitimate interest in keeping the service secure.</p>

    <h2>The data we collect and why</h2>
    <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Situation</th><th>Data</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis</th><th>Retention</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>You contact us (contact form)</td>
            <td>Name, email, company, expertise needed, message, attached brief (optional)</td>
            <td>Answer your request, propose profiles and a quote</td>
            <td>Pre-contractual steps taken at your request</td>
            <td>3 years after our last exchange</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>You sign up as a freelancer</td>
            <td>First name, last name, email, job, specialty, day rate, availability, references, notes, portfolio link, CV, photo and portfolio PDF (optional)</td>
            <td>Review your profile, offer you matching missions, present your profile to our clients</td>
            <td>Pre-contractual steps taken at your request</td>
            <td>While your profile is active, then 3 years after our last exchange</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Anonymized preview of your profile (freelancer)</td>
            <td>Job, expertise and main references, without name or contact details</td>
            <td>Showcase the network's profiles on the site and in our newsletters</td>
            <td>Legitimate interest; you can object when signing up (checkbox) or at any time</td>
            <td>Until you object or the profile is deleted</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Emails about your sign-up or availability (freelancer)</td>
            <td>First name, email, job</td>
            <td>Confirm your sign-up, check that your information is up to date</td>
            <td>Legitimate interest in keeping the network up to date; you can ask to stop receiving them</td>
            <td>Same as the profile</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>You are a client or prospect</td>
            <td>Business contact details, exchanges, proposals and mission documents</td>
            <td>Prepare and carry out our missions, invoice</td>
            <td>Contract, legal obligations (accounting)</td>
            <td>Duration of the relationship, then 3 years; accounting records 10 years</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>CVs you send are kept in a private storage space that only the digitags team can access. When a CV is shared with a client, we favor an anonymized version, through a link that expires after 7 days. We make no automated decisions producing legal effects concerning you. <strong>We do not sell or rent your data.</strong></p>

    <h2>Who can access your data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>The digitags team</strong>, only as far as needed to handle your request or offer you missions.</li>
      <li><strong>Our clients</strong>, for freelancers: only the information relevant to a given mission, preferably in anonymized form.</li>
      <li><strong>The companies of the <a href="/en/the-group">Digitags - Donutz group</a></strong>, when a project involves them.</li>
      <li><strong>Our technical processors</strong>, who act on our instructions:</li>
    </ul>
    <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Provider</th><th>Role</th><th>Data location</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Cloudflare, Inc. (United States)</td><td>Site hosting, security, internal notifications</td><td>Global network, including the United States</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Supabase, Inc. (United States)</td><td>Database and file storage (forms, profiles, CVs)</td><td>European Union (Sweden)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Resend (United States)</td><td>Emails sent to freelancers</td><td>European Union (Ireland)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Google (Google Workspace)</td><td>Team email</td><td>European Union and United States</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Plausible Insights OÜ (Estonia)</td><td>Cookieless audience measurement, no personal data</td><td>European Union</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Transfers outside the European Union</h2>
    <p>Some of our providers are US companies (Cloudflare, Google, Supabase, Resend). Even when data is hosted in the European Union, it may be accessed from the United States, for example for maintenance or support. These transfers are covered by the safeguards provided by the GDPR: the EU–US Data Privacy Framework for certified companies and, failing that, the standard contractual clauses adopted by the European Commission.</p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>The site is served over HTTPS only. CVs and internal documents are stored in a private space, protected by access rules that restrict them to the team. Document sharing links expire automatically, and commercial proposal pages can be password-protected.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You have the following rights over your data:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access</strong>: get a copy of the data we hold about you;</li>
      <li><strong>Rectification</strong>: correct inaccurate or incomplete data;</li>
      <li><strong>Erasure</strong>: ask us to delete your data, for example your freelancer profile;</li>
      <li><strong>Restriction</strong>: temporarily freeze the use of your data;</li>
      <li><strong>Objection</strong>: object to processing based on our legitimate interest, including the display of your anonymized profile or our emails;</li>
      <li><strong>Portability</strong>: receive the data you provided in a machine-readable format;</li>
      <li><strong>Withdrawal of consent</strong>, where processing is based on it;</li>
      <li><strong>Post-mortem instructions</strong>: decide what happens to your data after your death (French law).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To exercise them, email us at <a href={`mailto:${S.email}`}>{S.email}</a> or write to {S.denomination}, {S.siege}. We will reply within one month. We may ask you to prove your identity if we have reasonable doubts.</p>
    <p>If, after contacting us, you believe your rights are not respected, you can lodge a complaint with the French data protection authority, the <strong>CNIL</strong>: <a href="https://www.cnil.fr/en/home">www.cnil.fr</a> or 3 place de Fontenoy, TSA 80715, 75334 Paris Cedex 07, France.</p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>The site contains links to third-party sites, which apply their own privacy policies. We are not responsible for their practices.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy, for example if we add a service or a provider. The date of the last update appears at the top of this page.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
